# Project specific
# NOTE: must be `outputs/*`, not `outputs/`. Git cannot re-include a file
# once its parent directory is excluded, so with `outputs/` every `!` rule
# below was silently dead — which is why no results_summary_*.json ever
# reached the repo despite the exception.
outputs/*
!outputs/mailed_manifest_*.json
!outputs/results_summary_*.json
!outputs/telegram_manifest_*.json
# Accumulated match outcomes — the only durable record of settled results.
# Without this exception it stayed on the CI runner and was lost every run,
# which made the real-data backtest impossible.
!outputs/result_store.json
# settled_*.json is NOT tracked: it is derived from result_store.json by
# export_settled.py and regenerates in seconds. Committed once at 79 MB, which
# GitHub warns about and which buys nothing — result_store.json is the durable
# record, this is a view of it.
!outputs/scoring_calibration.json
!outputs/tennis_calibration.json
# The Dropping Odds workflow commits these; without the exception its
# `git add` was a silent no-op.
!outputs/oddssafari_dropping_*.json
*.log
scraper_log.txt
email_config.py
app_integration_config.json
gemini_config.py
groq_config.py

# Chrome driver logs
chromedriver.log

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.temp
.vercel
.env*.local
